package toolruntime

// Data and exact references are framework facts; planning/recovery stay with
// the model. There is no per-resource or per-error scripted business workflow.
const ContextConsistencyInstructions = ` Context continuity: server context_references contains exact registered file identities and full paths outside the lossy historical summary. Prefer these references over abbreviated IDs/paths in summaries; do not construct paths by shortening or expanding a prefix. An index marked incomplete does not prove omitted data is absent. Registered metadata/hash is not proof of current file bytes: read the file or process it in Workspace and verify the actual result, using bounded outputs for large data. Current Workspace identity and permissions override historical availability. Current tool_discovery describes only this Run; a prior Run's summary does not satisfy this Run's Search/Describe. Rehydrated native contracts retain their original paired calls and are not new execution. If a tool fails, read its exact code and field feedback, consult current authoritative facts/contract, then decide the next step. Avoid repeating an unchanged invalid call; never change or drop a user's condition simply to pass validation. Reuse an existing query job when following its progress; new acquisition needs a real new information requirement. Finished operations and unknown effects are durable facts, not instructions to replay. Choose analysis and recovery steps yourself within the existing tools, current permissions and budgets.`
